Installing {{ display_name }}
{{ '=' * (('Installing ' ~ display_name) | length) }}

{{ display_name }} comes as a VST3 and a CLAP plugin. Copy both from the folder for
your computer, then rescan plugins in your DAW. Use the CLAP version if
your DAW supports it.


macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel)
-------------------------------

1. In Finder, choose Go > Go to Folder and enter:
   ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins
2. Copy macOS/{{ display_name }}.vst3 into the VST3 folder.
3. Copy macOS/{{ display_name }}.clap into the CLAP folder.
   Create either folder if it isn’t there.

{{ display_name }} isn’t signed or notarized, so macOS may refuse to load it. If your
DAW doesn’t list it after a rescan, open Terminal, run this, then rescan:

   xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/{{ display_name }}.vst3 ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/CLAP/{{ display_name }}.clap


Windows
-------

Before unzipping, right-click the zip, choose Properties, check Unblock
and click OK. If SmartScreen or your antivirus blocks the download,
choose to keep it.

1. Copy Windows\{{ display_name }}.vst3 into:
   C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3
2. Copy Windows\{{ display_name }}.clap into:
   C:\Program Files\Common Files\CLAP
   Create either folder if it isn’t there.


Uninstalling
------------

Delete {{ display_name }}.vst3 and {{ display_name }}.clap from the folders above.
